Supreme Court · September 6, 2026
The administration asks the Supreme Court to lift a new block on mail-ballot rules
On Sunday the solicitor general filed application 26A305, asking the justices to pause a September 4 injunction of Postal Service ballot-mail rules. That injunction covers elections on or before November 3. Sunday's filing is 58 days before that election.
The story
Just the facts
Show the work
In this story
What happened
Why the judge blocked it
The catch
Where this sits
Who feels it
What the coverage got right, and what it got wrong
