Heading I
The Sunday application asks the Court to stay the September 4 injunction pending appeal to the First Circuit and any later petition, and it asks for an immediate administrative stay, a short pause while the justices decide the full request. Sauer writes that the rule imposes "modest envelope-design and addressee-information requirements", and that states remain responsible for who may vote by mail.
1
record
The injunction names Domestic Mail Manual sections 705.24.3.1, 705.24.3.2, 705.24.4.1, 705.24.4.2, 705.24.5.1, the first two sentences of 705.24.5.2, and 705.24.5.3(a), (b), and (c). Those are the envelope standards, portal registration and enrollment, and the noncompliance rules. It does not bar states from complying voluntarily. It does not enjoin the rule for elections after November 3.
