Where this sits
Who pays
Mail voters in the plaintiff states.
The September 4 order binds the Postal Service defendants for elections on or before November 3. It does not limit that command to the plaintiff states. Sauer told the Court North Carolina had already begun mailing, Alabama would on September 9, and at least five states the week of September 13. If the stay is granted, election offices sending non-UOCAVA outbound ballots would face the portal and envelope rules while some of those mailings are already moving. Why it matters: the next order lands on those offices and the voters waiting on outbound ballots, not only on voters in the states that sued, and not on UOCAVA ballots the rule excludes.
