That wording checks out. USPS 820.225 is a federal Privacy Act system at Postal Service headquarters and a supplier cloud environment. It records names, addresses, issuing states, and barcodes, keeps them for five years, and states a law-enforcement purpose. State and local officials load the rows. It is not a citizenship file.
