0199	The catch
0200	Told versus record
0201	The block is of the rule, not the order.
0202	The Associated Press, PBS NewsHour, and CNBC wrote that Talwani extended an order against the Postal Service "enforcing President Donald Trump's executive order." CBS wrote "enforcing President Trump's executive order." The September 4 injunction names sections of the Postal Service rule issued August 21 and published August 26. The Court's August 24 stay had already paused her earlier injunction of the executive order itself. Why it matters: a reader of those dispatches can think the justices are being asked to revive the March order, when the fight before the Court is the Postal Service's published rule.
