   177	                       IDENTITY AND INTEREST OF AMICUS 1
   178	
   179	        Amicus Whistleblower Aid is a nonpartisan, nonprofit legal services
   180	
   181	organization dedicated to supporting and protecting whistleblowers for the public
   182	
   183	interest in pursuit of a robust, resilient, and thriving democracy. Whistleblower Aid
   184	
   185	provides pro bono representation to government and private-sector workers who
   186	
   187	report and expose wrongdoing—safely, lawfully, and responsibly. 2
   188	
   189	        Whistleblower        Aid    represents      an     anonymous        federal     official    (the
   190	
   191	“Whistleblower”) who has direct knowledge of the potentially catastrophic problems
   192	
   193	with the United States Postal Service’s (“USPS” or “Postal Service”) new procedures,
   194	
   195	policies, and information technology tools (together, the “systems”) for handling
   196	
   197	outgoing federal election ballot mail (“ballot mail”). 3 Those systems, including the
   198	
   199	USPS’ “Federal Ballot Mail Portal” and related information technology, are supposed
   200	
   201	to be used to implement 39 C.F.R. pt. 111, the rule promulgated by USPS under
   202	
   203	Section 3 of Exec. Order No. 14399, “Ensuring Citizenship Verification and Integrity
   204	
   205	in Federal Elections,” 91 Fed. Reg. 17125 (Mar. 31, 2026) (“Executive Order” or
   206	
   207	“Order”).
