   215	the preparation or submission of this brief. No person other than the amicus curiae or its counsel made
   216	a monetary contribution to its preparation or submission.
   217	2 For more information on amicus, see Whistleblower Aid, https://whistlebloweraid.org/ (last visited
   218	
   219	Sept. 8, 2026).
   220	3 USPS defines “ballot mail” as any mailpiece sent to or from an authorized election official containing
   221	
   222	a live ballot that may be used to cast a vote in an election. USPS, Election Mail, https://perma.cc/K2ED-
   223	JFEQ (last visited Sept. 8, 2026). Outgoing ballot mail refers to blank ballots mailed to voters.
