TsW AMhAA daRVX ISNQ sKyCY eRftA acPPc ebfE nFwaT MCnQE mEeeY SmBjI xegrY VvTxJ iulOd NIuqO zzscu lzDCc aHUBM hbvnu OjMNy eQqcx SVqKB GQmdz jaoD iShaE ONJdw vrZxD OnRTz gbbfF roDbV kRoBe oMlSS gfNzt oJhud eXZcf zhVlX "><div class="XQpSH zzkIM UtCfs sXthe lyRMG " data-testid="prism-divider"></div><div><div class="liAe uMOq zYIfP pYgZk Mxrkk hsDdd lZur TPpRg NoUSU igcMP DtJWr QgBvn DFdlJ " data-testid="prism-card"><div class="QGHKv iVcn avodi rEPuv ICwhc ibBnq seFhp WtEci "><div class="jOnhj VZTD nkdHX mLASH UbGlr QdTDD agITg bpqt mHqho hsWBK oxlKP lJgFA Rnzzu Laoga tbaWd LCaAL sYXyQ lgVFM "><a class="pbxMg VXYVd cgQhr SreVq UCWTg yjKUh ujbQC FZFZV EoRHR " href="https://abcnews.com/Politics/federal-judge-temporarily-blocks-trump-administrations-attempt-restrict/story?id=136021374" tabindex="0"><div class="oQtGj FfGkL hfDkF ICQCm ">Related</div><div class="TOZgg OBbQX VwBPh ">Federal judge temporarily blocks Trump administration&#x27;s attempt to restrict mail-in voting</div></a><div><a class="VZTD jIRH mLASH Cxsnp hyWKA BPJf CFZbp XICbf ndtbj xmxeG " href="https://abcnews.com/Politics/federal-judge-temporarily-blocks-trump-administrations-attempt-restrict/story?id=136021374"><div class="VZTD jIRH mLASH dpDOL cYfNW EnbxU iYmJ IwkEF "><svg aria-hidden="true" class="prism-Iconography prism-Iconography--arrows-rightArrow" focusable="false" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><path fill="currentColor" d="M15 1.6c-.9.9-.9 2.3 0 3.1l9.5 9.5H2.2c-1.2 0-2.2 1-2.2 2.2 0 1.2 1 2.2 2.2 2.2h22.3L15 28.1c-.9.9-.9 2.3 0 3.1.9.9 2.3.9 3.1 0L31.4 18c.9-.9.9-2.3 0-3.1L18.1 1.6c-.8-.9-2.2-.9-3.1 0z"></path></svg></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div class="XQpSH zzkIM UtCfs Ufjyt " data-testid="prism-divider"></div></div><p class="EkqkG IGXmU nlgHS yuUao lqtkC TjIXL aGjvy ">In its latest appeal to the justices,<strong class="vtkaO "> </strong>the Trump administration insisted the rules impose only &quot;modest&quot; ballot design and review requirements on states and that a requirement to submit name, address, and barcode information of intended recipients is not onerous or intrusive.<!-- --> </p><div class="oLzSq QrHMO GbsKS pvsTF EhJPu vPlOC zNYgW OsTsW AMhAA daRVX ISNQ sKyCY eRftA acPPc ebfE nFwaT MCnQE mEeeY SmBjI xegrY VvTxJ iulOd NIuqO zzscu lzDCc aHUBM hbvnu OjMNy eQqcx SVqKB GQmdz jaoD iShaE ONJdw vrZxD OnRTz gbbfF roDbV kRoBe oMlSS gfNzt oJhud eXZcf zhVlX "><div data-testid="prism-ad-wrapper" style="min-height:250px;transition:min-height 0.3s linear 0s" data-ad-placeholder="true"><div data-box-type="fitt-adbox-fitt-article-inline-box" data-testid="prism-ad"><div class="Ad fitt-article-inline-box  ad-slot  " data-slot-type="fitt-article-inline-box" data-slot-kvps="pos=fitt-article-inline-box"></div></div></div></div><p class="EkqkG IGXmU nlgHS yuUao lqtkC TjIXL aGjvy ">The states challenging the USPS rule have until Tuesday, Sept. 8, at 10 a.m. to formally respond before the Supreme Court makes a decision.<!-- --> </p><p class="EkqkG IGXmU nlgHS yuUao lqtkC eTIW sUzSN ">The states and voter advocacy groups have argued that the new USPS regulations are an attempt by the Trump administration to federalize elections, which are historically and constitutionally managed by each state, and make it harder to vote by mail for everyday citizens.</p></div><div><div data-testid="prism-tags"><h2 class="QOIir HJolv pZjYK JKlkC RZhHM ">Related Topics</h2><ul class="VZTD UeCOM dAmzA ltDkr qBPOY uoPjL "><li class=" "><a class="theme-xFEdM theme-HReFq mLASH egFzk qXWHA ScoIf zYXIH jIRH qoFvU OJpwZ eqFg wSPfd ofvJb jsJUp LaUnX EgONj ibBnq kyjTO lvyBv aANqO aNnIu GDslh LjPJo UDizh gHvnI RpDvg PdXI rTpcz EDgo SIwmX oIWqB mzm MbcTC sXtkB yayQB vXSTR ENhiS dQa-Du SVBll bpBbX GpQCA tuAKv xTell wdAqb ZqGqs LVAIE TnrRA uECag DcwSV SFxVK RLguq JlrmG mTvxX BGtAO XnBOJ cELRj SUAFz XzYk zkmjG aSyef GxrZt MiRQN RydZZ pFen hoNVj TQOOL eqzUB ThfLp WMSMl Haltu NafGB KpEhF pECQM q