src/pages/events/mail-voting/september-2026.astro:213:        <p data-layer="narrative">If you vote by mail this cycle, the injunction is what keeps the Postal Service from treating noncompliant outbound mailings presented by election offices as unaccepted mail for elections on or before November 3. Return ballots from voters are outside section 705.24.5. If the Court stays that injunction, offices sending non-UOCAVA outbound ballots would have to meet the envelope and portal rules while some of those mailings are already moving. Sauer's own line is that once envelopes "enter the mailstream, there is no retrieving them."<Cite s="scotus-26a305-application" passage="there is no retrieving them" /><Cite s="usps-final-rule" passage="does not apply to Return Federal Ballot Mail" /></p>
