 succeeded in 116ms:
     1	David Steiner
     2	August 31, 2026
     3	Page 1
     4	
     5	
     6	
     7	
     8	                                                 August 31, 2026
     9	
    10	VIA ELECTRONIC MAIL
    11	David Steiner
    12	Postmaster General and Chief Executive Officer
    13	United States Postal Service
    14	475 L’Enfant Plaza SW
    15	Washington, DC 20260
    16	
    17	Dear Postmaster General Steiner,
    18	
    19	        My office is in receipt of an alarming whistleblower disclosure (the “Disclosure”)
    20	outlining the United States Postal Service’s (“USPS”) perilously rushed and potentially unlawful
    21	implementation of President Trump’s Executive Order seeking to restrict mail-in voting. 1 The
    22	whistleblower’s allegations make clear that USPS lacks the technical or operational capability
    23	needed to effectively implement the EO’s provisions in a way that safeguards every citizen’s
    24	right to vote in the upcoming midterm elections. Despite this, the Trump Administration appears
    25	intent on USPS moving forward with its flawed plans, no matter the chaos they may create. 2 The
    26	whistleblower’s allegations also provide disturbing information suggesting that USPS may have
    27	violated a court order by continuing to implement the EO despite being ordered to cease all such
    28	work. We urge you to abandon this ill-conceived, unconscionable plan and ensure that all
    29	Americans can exercise their constitutional right to vote, including by mail, without interference
    30	by USPS.
    31	
    32	         Historically, although USPS has issued guidance on various issues related to election
    33	ballots sent through the mail, like recommendations for ballot envelope design, it has not
    34	imposed specific rules or procedures that state election officials were required to follow in order
    35	to have USPS deliver ballot mail to voters. Under a new final rule issued on August 26, 2026 (the
    36	“Rule”), USPS will, for the first time, play a gatekeeping function and be in a position to refuse
    37	to mail ballots that state election officials have determined should be sent out. 3 This change is a
    38	marked and deeply troubling departure from USPS’s traditionally restrained role as a mail
    39	carrier.
    40	
    41	       The whistleblower’s Disclosure describes an unprecedented process that allows USPS to
    42	decide whether ballots issued by state election officials should be mailed. To do so, USPS is
    43	building an entirely new online system, the USPS Federal Ballot Mail Portal and related IT
    44	
