   497	10.​Prior to this rule, as in past elections, election ballot mail was essentially handled
   498	    like other bulk First-Class Mail mailings. Nothing close to the extent and severity of
   499	    this new USPS system and attendant processes seems to have existed before. In
   500	    the past, for these mailings of ballot mail that were brought to a BMEU (“Business
   501	    Mail Entry Unit”), the mailer would enter the information into a digital system like
   502	    PostalOne!, which would generate a manifest-like document.12 While the Postal
   503	    Service has subjected large mailings to validation processes before they were
   504	    accepted, those processes appeared generally to be focused on collecting proper
   505	    postage rates. Such processes appeared designed not to stop mailing, but instead
   506	    allow the Postal Service to properly bill the mailer at the appropriate rate.13 And of
   507	    those processes reviewed, some like Bundle Verification allowed for a 20% failure
   508	    rate.14 We found no evidence in reviewing the processes for a zero percent failure
   509	    rate for individual pieces of mail, or for the creation of a manifest to be checked
   510	    against some sort of other mailer generated document (akin to the list that election
   511	    officials are required to enter into the Portal), or any published failure rate for
   512	    election ballot mail.
