  3150	feedback to mailers within 2 business
  3151	days after receiving the mailer’s request
  3152	and necessary information and samples.
  3153	More information about the MDA
  3154	review process is available in Kit 600 or
  3155	at https://postalpro.usps.com/node/773.
  3156	E. Federal Ballot Mail Portal
  3157	Under 705.24.4, Federal Ballot Mail
  3158	Portal Users, including state and local
  3159	election officials and other authorized
  3160	users, such as MSPs, must submit
  3161	certain data into the Federal Ballot Mail
  3162	Portal prior to presenting an Outbound
  3163	Federal Ballot mailing for acceptance.
  3164	Chief state election officials are not
  3165	required to enter this data themselves or
  3166	to consolidate data for all political
  3167	subdivisions within their state before
  3168	data can be entered into the Portal. The
  3169	chief state election official of each state
  3170	does, however, authorize access for
  3171	other Federal Ballot Mail Portal Users
  3172	within their state. The rule also allows
  3173	other individuals to enter information
  3174	into the Portal if authorized, such as
  3175	staff members, MSPs, or other vendors,
  3176	thereby minimizing any potential
  3177	administrative burden on election
  3178	officials.
  3179	The Postal Service recognizes that
  3180	many states have decentralized election
  3181	administration. It is important that the
  3182	state, through the chief state election
  3183	official, maintain ultimate control over
  3184	access to the Portal because they will
  3185	have more visibility into their own
  3186	election structures than will the Postal
  3187	Service.
  3188	Voters themselves will not enroll with
  3189	the Postal Service, and are not
  3190	responsible for verifying Portal
  3191	information or correcting information
  3192	provided by Federal Ballot Mail Portal
  3193	Users. In part, this is because voters do
  3194	not design ballot mail envelopes and,
  3195	consequently, do not have the relevant
  3196	data elements for the Portal. Instead,
  3197	that responsibility lies exclusively with
  3198	election officials and their authorized
  3199	MSPs.
  3200	Once Federal Ballot Mail Portal Users
  3201	have set up a Portal account, they will
  3202	be prompted to certify that their
  3203	Outbound and Return Federal Ballot
  3204	Mail envelopes have been submitted for
  3205	MDA review and that they have
  3206	received feedback. Federal Ballot Mail
  3207	Portal Users will not be able to upload
  3208	any data into the Portal until the
  3209	certification is complete. This will
  3210	ensure compliance with DMM
  3211	705.24.3.1 and 705.24.3.2 and reduces
  3212	the information that is verified prior to
  3213	acceptance of an Outbound Federal
