  3378	The ability to add and amend lists
  3379	also allows Authorized Ballot Mailers to
  3380	enter Outbound Federal Ballot Mail in
  3381	batches, consistent with the current
  3382	practice for many in the election
  3383	community. Federal Ballot Mail Portal
  3384	Users may continue to supplement the
  3385	Portal data as permitted by state law,
  3386	potentially up until Election Day. The
  3387	only constraint imposed by the rule in
  3388	this regard is that the information for a
  3389	particular mailing must be uploaded
  3390	into the Portal prior to the Outbound
  3391	Federal Ballot mailing being presented
  3392	to the Postal Service for acceptance.
  3393	Thus, the Portal and verification process
  3394	accommodate election officials who (for
  3395	example) may do one large mailing and
  3396	multiple smaller mailings. It also
  3397	accommodates election officials who
  3398	prepare many ballots for mailing at once
  3399	but enter them into the mailstream in
  3400	multiple installments.
  3401	Portal data will be updated as soon as
  3402	it is submitted by the Federal Ballot
  3403	Mail Portal User, and there should be
  3404	minimal to no delay between Portal
  3405	upload and a mailer’s ability to present
  3406	the mailing for acceptance. Portal data
  3407	will also be available for verification
  3408	purposes on a nationwide basis. If an
  3409	Outbound Federal Ballot mailing is
  3410	presented for acceptance outside of the
  3411	issuing state, Postal Service employees
  3412	would still have access to the necessary
  3413	Portal data to perform verification under
  3414	DMM 705.24.5.
  3415	Within the Portal, the Postal Service
  3416	plans to confirm that the required data
  3417	fields are completed (i.e., they may not
  3418	be left blank) prior to Outbound Federal
  3419	Ballot mailings being presented for
  3420	acceptance. This includes verifying the
  3421	unique IMb on Return Federal Ballot
  3422	Mail has been uploaded into the Portal.
  3423	Aside from confirming that the required
  3424	data has been uploaded, however, the
  3425	Postal Service will not otherwise verify,
  3426	correct, or amend any data entered into
  3427	the Portal. It will not determine whether
  3428	an individual’s name is accurate; so, for
  3429	example, married women changing their
  3430	names or potential mismatches for
  3431	misspellings will not prevent a ballot
  3432	from reaching a voter under the rule.
  3433	Likewise, the Postal Service will not
  3434	assess the accuracy of the address
  3435	entered, such as to determine whether
  3436	there is a Change of Address or whether
  3437	the address is otherwise invalid.
  3438	Moreover, the address uploaded into the
  3439	Portal should be the address used on the
  3440	Outbound Federal Ballot Mail envelope.
  3441	Nontraditional addresses, such as tribal
  3442	addresses, college dormitories, and
  3443	long-term care facilities, can and should
  3444	be entered into the Portal if that is the
  3445	address on the Outbound Federal Ballot
  3446	envelope. Voters who may move often,
