  3482	official voter rolls.
  3483	Finally, shortly after the effective date
  3484	of the final rule, the Postal Service will
  3485	make additional guidance documents
  3486	available, including a User Guide for the
  3487	Portal and Technical Specifications for
  3488	the Portal. These resources will explain
  3489	how to create a Portal account, how to
  3490	assign and approve Federal Ballot Mail
  3491	Portal Users, the file format for Portal
  3492	uploads, and how to resolve errors and
  3493	make new submissions; these
  3494	documents will be available in
  3495	accessible formats. The Postal Service
  3496	has an established process for
  3497	communicating new or updated
  3498	technical requirements that it will
  3499	deploy to inform election officials,
  3500	MSPs, and others in the mailing
  3501	community about the Portal and these
  3502	resources. This process includes
  3503	familiar communications channels,
  3504	including Industry Alerts and Mailers
  3505	Technical Advisory Committee User
  3506	Group notifications, which help to
  3507	ensure that the information reaches the
  3508	appropriate audience. MCRs are also
  3509	available to assist individual customers
  3510	by email and phone. The Postal Service
  3511	will also directly engage with election
  3512	officials, MSPs, and other stakeholders
  3513	to answer questions and provide
  3514	guidance related to implementation of
  3515	the rule.
  3516	F. Outbound Federal Ballot Mail Entry
  3517	When preparing Outbound Federal
  3518	Ballot mailings, Authorized Ballot
  3519	Mailers must segregate Outbound
  3520	Federal Ballot Mail from other types of
  3521	ballot mail, such as primary ballots,
  3522	UOCAVA ballots, or ballots for state or
  3523	local elections only. Comingling non-
