  3531	federal ballot mail with Outbound
  3532	Federal Ballot Mail may impact the
  3533	verification process and could prevent
  3534	or delay proper acceptance of mailings.
  3535	For ballots that have both federal and
  3536	state issues on the ballot, the mailing
  3537	will be treated as Outbound Federal
  3538	Ballot Mail and will be subject to the
  3539	rule. At entry, mailers should inform the
  3540	BMEU technician or Retail clerk if a
  3541	ballot mailing contains non-federal
  3542	ballots. Timing differences (between
  3543	primaries and general elections or
  3544	between federal and state elections) and
  3545	external indicia may also help alert
  3546	postal employees to the presence of
  3547	non-Federal Ballot Mail.
  3548	The Postal Service is also working on
  3549	establishing Federal Election Mail and
  3550	Non-Federal Election Mail Service Type
  3551	Identifiers (‘‘STIDs’’). Specifically, the
  3552	Postal Service is planning to convert the
  3553	current Election Mail STIDs to Federal
  3554	Election Mail STIDs. New STIDs will be
  3555	developed for non-Federal elections.
  3556	This approach will assist jurisdictions
  3557	that may have already finalized the
  3558	printing process for their 2026 general
  3559	election envelopes relying on the
  3560	existing STID table, and will support
  3561	their ability to comply with the final
  3562	rule. Having unique STIDs for Federal
  3563	and non-Federal elections will help to
  3564	further distinguish Federal Ballot Mail
  3565	from other ballot mail. Prior to
  3566	finalizing and releasing the new STIDs,
  3567	the Postal Service will publish a notice
  3568	in the Federal Register.
  3569	As stated in the proposed rule,
  3570	Outbound Federal Ballot mailings must
  3571	be entered at a Post Office retail counter,
  3572	including manual post offices, or a
  3573	BMEU. A locator tool for Postal Service
  3574	locations is available here: https://
  3575	tools.usps.com/locations/. These
  3576	mailings may not be entered into blue
  3577	collection boxes, collection boxes in
  3578	retail lobbies, or through other means.
  3579	While the rule makes this restriction
  3580	mandatory, it is also consistent with the
  3581	Postal Service’s general guidance for
  3582	outbound ballot mailings. Commercial
  3583	mailings must meet applicable DMM
  3584	requirements. Mailings paid at singlepiece First Class Mail rates are not
  3585	required to meet commercial mailing
  3586	standards.
  3587	Verification under 705.24.5 will be
  3588	performed at a BMEU or Post Office
  3589	retail counter when an Outbound
  3590	Federal Ballot mailing is presented for
  3591	acceptance. Conducting verification
  3592	prior to acceptance is intended to
  3593	obviate confusion and provide a clear,
  3594	immediate identification of potential
  3595	issues. Either a BMEU technician, if the
  3596	mailing is presented at a BMEU, or
  3597	Retail clerk, if the mailing is presented
  3598	at a Post Office or other Postal Service
