  5639	Definitions
  5640	
  5641	For the purposes of Section 705.24,
  5642	the following definitions apply:
  5643	a. Authorized ballot mailer means an
  5644	election official of a state or a political
  5645	subdivision thereof who is responsible
  5646	for sending mail-in or absentee ballots
  5647	to eligible voters of that state or political
  5648	subdivision; or an individual or entity,
  5649	such as a mail service provider, that an
  5650	election official has authorized to send
  5651	mail-in or absentee ballots by mail on
  5652	the election official’s behalf.
  5653	b. Federal Ballot Mail Portal User
  5654	means the chief election official of each
  5655	state and any individual or entity, such
  5656	as a mail service provider or an election
  5657	official of that state or a political
  5658	subdivision thereof, authorized by the
  5659	chief election official to provide
