  6101	SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:
  6102	I. Executive Summary
  6103	A. What is the Agency’s authority for
  6104	taking this action?
  6105	TSCA section 5(a)(2) (15 U.S.C.
  6106	2604(a)(2)) authorizes EPA to determine
  6107	that a use of a chemical substance is a
  6108	‘‘significant new use.’’ EPA must make
  6109	this determination by rule after
  6110	considering all relevant factors,
  6111	including the factors in TSCA section
  6112	5(a)(2).
  6113	B. What action is the Agency taking?
  6114	EPA is finalizing SNURs under TSCA
  6115	section 5(a)(2) for the chemical
  6116	substances identified in this document.
  6117	These chemical substances were the
  6118	subject of PMNs and are also subject to
  6119	an Order issued by EPA pursuant to
  6120	TSCA section 5(e)(1)(A), as required by
  6121	the determinations made under TSCA
  6122	section 5(a)(3)(B). The SNURs identify
  6123	as significant new uses any
  6124	manufacturing, processing, use,
  6125	distribution in commerce, or disposal
  6126	that does not conform to the restrictions
  6127	imposed by the underlying TSCA
  6128	Orders, consistent with TSCA section
  6129	5(f)(4). The SNURs require persons who
  6130	intend to manufacture or process any of
  6131	these chemical substances for an
  6132	activity that is designated as a
  6133	significant new use in the SNURs to
  6134	notify EPA at least 90 days before
  6135	commencing that activity.
  6136	Previously, EPA proposed SNURs for
  6137	these chemical substances in the
  6138	Federal Register of November 3, 2025
  6139	(90 FR 49148 (FRL–12742–01–OCSPP)).
  6140	The docket includes information
  6141	considered by the Agency in developing
  6142	the proposed and final rules, including
  6143	public comments and EPA’s responses
