  1450	
  1451	
  1452	
  1453	
  1454	(“[S]tate law is preempted by federal statute only so far as the conflict extends.”) (quotation
  1455	
  1456	omitted). Accordingly, the court finds Plaintiffs likely to succeed on their claim that the Final
  1457	
  1458	Rule is an election rule where it purports to regulate the time, place, and manner of elections and
  1459	
  1460	is unconstitutional where Congress has not authorized such a rule under the Elections Clause.
