  1549	   Given the distribution of authority over elections, see supra Section III.B.1, it is worth noting
  1550	that clear authorization is particularly needed where “an agency seeks to intrude into an area that
  1551	is the particular domain of state law” and “risks intruding on powers reserved to the States.” See
  1552	West Virginia v. EPA, 597 U.S. 697, 744 (Gorsuch, J., concurring) (quotation omitted). Courts
  1553	“require Congress to enact exceedingly clear language if it wishes to significantly alter the
  1554	balance between federal and state power.” United States Forest Serv. v. Cowpasture River
  1555	Preservation Assn., 590 U.S. 604, 621–22 (2020).
