  6028	SUMMARY: EPA is issuing significant new
  6029	
  6030	use rules (SNURs) under the Toxic
  6031	Substances Control Act (TSCA) for
  6032	certain chemical substances that were
  6033	the subject of premanufacture notices
  6034	(PMNs) and are also subject to an Order
  6035	issued by EPA pursuant to TSCA. The
  6036	SNURs require persons to notify EPA at
  6037	least 90 days before commencing the
  6038	manufacture (defined by statute to
  6039	include import) or processing of any of
  6040	these chemical substances for an
  6041	activity that is designated as a
  6042	significant new use in the SNUR. The
  6043	required notification initiates EPA’s
  6044	evaluation of the conditions of that use
  6045	for that chemical substance. In addition,
  6046	the manufacture or processing for the
  6047	significant new use may not commence
  6048	until EPA has conducted a review of the
  6049	required notification; made an
  6050	appropriate determination regarding
  6051	that notification; and taken such actions
  6052	as required by that determination.
