  4385	C. Balancing Interests
  4386	After careful consideration of these
  4387	various viewpoints, and the comments
  4388	discussing these issues, the Postal
  4389	Service is moving to finalize the
  4390	proposed rule, subject to certain
  4391	modifications explained in ‘‘Revisions
  4392	Adopted in the Final Rule.’’
  4393	The Postal Service has thoroughly
  4394	explained the rationale for imposing
  4395	mail preparation and data reporting
  4396	requirements as set forth in the
  4397	proposed rule, which are necessary to
  4398	help promote the faithful execution of
  4399	federal law and advance the Postal
  4400	Service’s ability to efficiently handle
  4401	Federal Ballot Mail. While the Postal
  4402	Service’s existing processes are
  4403	designed to support the timely delivery
  4404	and smooth processing of ballot mail, it
  4405	has long recognized that across-theboard compliance with its longstanding
  4406	recommendations would further
  4407	improve efficient handling, processing,
  4408	and delivery. This would benefit the
  4409	Postal Service, election officials, and
  4410	voters alike. Moreover, while the Postal
  4411	Service currently does obtain scan data
  4412	for some ballot mail that could be useful
  4413	for law-enforcement purposes,
  4414	mandating compliance with the data
  4415	reporting and mail-preparation
  4416	requirements for all Federal Ballot Mail
  4417	would significantly improve the quality
  4418	of that data. This visibility will, in turn,
  4419	put law enforcement in a better position
  4420	to identify any potential issues
  4421	regarding compliance with federal law
  4422	that may merit further investigation.
  4423	Weighing these benefits and the
  4424	operational needs of the Postal Service,
