80-       Not only is this system astonishingly untested, USPS has simultaneously implemented an
81:impracticable zero percent failure rate. 13 When ballots are submitted to USPS in large-volume
82:batches, if any one ballot in the batch cannot be verified against the Portal, all ballots in that
83:batch will be rejected. For example, if a state election official brings a batch of 10,000 ballots to
84:USPS and USPS is unable to match just one of those ballots against the Portal – because, for
85-example, someone has recently changed their name after marriage or they’ve moved – then
86-USPS would refuse to mail the remaining 9,999 ballots as well. As the whistleblower notes,
