696:23.​When an election worker uploads a ballot mail batch manifest into the legacy bulk
697-    mail systems, USPS will run the first ballot mail verification process which could
698-    delay election officials and ballot delivery. This new automated verification process
699-    will compare the IMb details in the batch manifest against the Statewide List
700:    provided in the Portal. Additionally, the manifest verification process will confirm if
701-    the proper federal or state/local ballot indicators are included. If manifest data is
702:    complete and the IMbs match those found in the Portal, the State is authorized to
703-    bring the ballots to a USPS location which can receive and mail the ballots.23 If the
704-    manifest verification fails, election officials will not be authorized to bring their ballot
705:    mail to the Postal Service. This is the first point of failure where state ballot mail can
706-    be held up.
