f4ef52ecc747"><h3>Portal availability</h3><p class="ledger-excerpt" data-source-copy>Meanwhile, USPS submitted a declaration to the district court today explaining that the Portal is not yet functional and will not be available until, at the earliest, “sometime next week.”</p><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:2d87991b16bc379bd0b08e0377848e56c394460fd80bfa94bd39d29bd5cc1523/" data-passage="Meanwhile, USPS submitted a declaration to the district court today explaining that the Portal is not yet functional and will not be available until, at the earliest, “sometime next week.”" aria-label="Read the source for Portal availability">State of California <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-55fab761-7712-4577-b036-ad75ef9eb8d7"><h3>TRO expiration</h3><p class="ledger-excerpt" data-source-copy>The First Circuit has before it a motion for a stay of the TRO pending appeal on which highly expedited briefing is already complete.</p><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:2d87991b16bc379bd0b08e0377848e56c394460fd80bfa94bd39d29bd5cc1523/" data-passage="The First Circuit has before it a motion for a stay of the TRO pending appeal on which highly expedited briefing is already complete." aria-label="Read the source for TRO expiration">State of California <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-7bafa508-8a5e-4c4f-bbf9-013e45fbb1b8"><h3>Administrative stay duration</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:dea1c24ad24a3ba6b98f4fb030624477959140608a8932834a382dbe57889776-9317490398081991" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="7" data-figure-unit="days">7 days</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:dea1c24ad24a3ba6b98f4fb030624477959140608a8932834a382dbe57889776/" data-passage="On July 7, 2026, the district court granted a seven-day administrative" aria-label="Read the source for Administrative stay duration">U.S. Department of Justice, Office of the Solicitor General <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>On July 7, 2026, the district court granted a seven-day administrative</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-aabeb048-bfe3-43cc-8510-c44829e6d944"><h3>Injunction status</h3><p>This record does not yet establish one current value.</p></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-a93f0ba6-d11e-4a21-8439-2be2b15cc291"><h3>TRO status</h3><p class="ledger-excerpt" data-source-copy>(2) Defendants’ counsel must, within 24 hours after receiving service of this Order: (i) provide written notice of this Order to the USPS Defendants and their employees; (ii) notify all such recipients that they are required to comply with this Order, under penalty of contempt; and (iii) file on the docket by the next business day a copy of the notice and/or communications referred to in (i)–(ii).</p><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384/" data-passage="(2) Defendants’ counsel must, within 24 hours after receiving service of this Order: (i) provide written notice of this Order to the USPS Defendants and their employees; (ii) notify all such recipients that they are required to comply with this Order, under penalty of contempt; and (iii) file on the docket by the next business day a copy of the notice and/or communications referred to in (i)–(ii)." aria-label="Read the source for TRO status">U.S. District Court for the District of Massachusetts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-22b3ccdd-bbd4-42ca-bc88-ca3c8ba5cc17"><h3>Comment count</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384-d16c6c9cdba01273" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="over 200000" data-figure-unit="comments">over 200000 comments</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384/" data-passage="The USPS reported that it had received over 200,000 comments from citizens; postal unions; federal, state, local, and tribal officials; election officials; voting rights organizations; and other issue-based and political advocacy groups." aria-label="Read the source for Comment count">U.S. District Court for the District of Massachusetts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>The USPS reported that it had received over 200,000 comments from citizens; postal unions; federal, state, local, and tribal officials; election officials; voting rights organizations; and other issue-based and political advocacy groups.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-f0006ed0-fa06-4f54-b785-9cdc01830720"><h3>TRO duration</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384-202572aabdfd5838" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="14" data-figure-unit="days">14 days</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384/" data-passage="On August 27, 2026, the court granted a temporary restraining order (“TRO”), enjoining USPS from implementing mandatory sections of the Final Rule for fourteen days." aria-label="Read the source for TRO duration">U.S. District Court for the District of Massachusetts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>On August 27, 2026, the court granted a temporary restraining order (“TRO”), enjoining USPS from implementing mandatory sections of the Final Rule for fourteen days.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-86547571-c65e-42e7-8943-1f8f94216bc8"><h3>Application deadline</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc-dc05d33a2a637357" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="30" data-figure-unit="days">30 days</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc/" data-passage="(2) accept and process, with respect to any election for Federal office, any otherwise valid voter registration application and absentee ballot application from an absent uniformed services voter or overseas voter, if the application is received by the appropriate State election official not less than 30 days before the election;" aria-label="Read the source for Application deadline">Office of the Law Revision Counsel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>(2) accept and process, with respect to any election for Federal office, any otherwise valid voter registration application and absentee ballot application from an absent uniformed services voter or overseas voter, if the application is received by the appropriate State election official not less than 30 days before the election;</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-4e2bf72c-b70d-4660-b7e4-72100d79f0b0"><h3>Ballot transmission deadline</h3><p>This record does not yet establish one current value.</p></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-5d117c91-3f9c-4ffd-91e9-0ebdc2b2e978"><h3>Report deadline</h3><p>This record does not yet establish one current value.</p></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-ff9e64af-4f84-42e0-b772-698eb61f884e"><h3>Electronic channels</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc-5553f811c3831c7b" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="1" data-figure-unit="means of electronic communication">1 means of electronic communication</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc/" data-passage="Each State shall, in addition to the designation of a single State office under subsection (b), designate not less than 1 means of electronic communication-" aria-label="Read the source for Electronic channels">Office of the Law Revision Counsel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>Each State shall, in addition to the designation of a single State office under subsection (b), designate not less than 1 means of electronic communication-</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-92670ab1-03dc-49e0-abdf-9b91062326b5"><h3>Waiver decision deadline</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc-9a873f108949c9ca" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="5" data-figure-unit="business days">5 business days</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc/" data-passage="The Presidential designee shall approve or deny the waiver request not later than 5 business days after the date on which the request is received." aria-label="Read the source for Waiver decision deadline">Office of the Law Revision Counsel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>The Presidential designee shall approve or deny the waiver request not later than 5 business days after the date on which the request is received.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-addbc417-e39a-499f-808a-3c77eb796c59"><h3>Supreme Court appeals</h3><p>This record does not yet establish one current value.</p></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-d3f6993b-9aa3-4e3f-88d4-902eff5ddc9a"><h3>Prior Supreme Court requests</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:e76df51c715bb605096df8547c9411804fdb08f4ff4b83a117cc2456baf4127b-f12e4df86c8ac8a8" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="2" data-figure-unit="times">2 times</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:e76df51c715bb605096df8547c9411804fdb08f4ff4b83a117cc2456baf4127b/" data-passage="Sunday’s application to the Supreme Court comes after the Trump administration already twice asked the highest court to intervene in this case." aria-label="Read the source for Prior Supreme Court requests">NBC News <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>Sunday’s application to the Supreme Court comes after the Trump administration already twice asked the highest court to intervene in this case.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-46cf35f9-91c2-41fe-bbab-759d07cf31de"><h3>Application length</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:2784b5d2da64e012b920da0a0d37bbe3b7e60179e56e8d0ad0cdbfbdfcefdf52-ef727bec358d7c7e" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="40" data-figure-unit="pages">40 pages</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:2784b5d2da64e012b920da0a0d37bbe3b7e60179e56e8d0ad0cdbfbdfcefdf52/" data-passage="In a 40-page emergency application, Solicitor General D. John Sauer asked the justices to immediately permit the administration to bar the U.S. Postal Service from sending mail-in ballots to residents of states that have not submitted a list of eligible voters based on citizenship data." aria-label="Read the source for Application length">The Hill <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>In a 40-page emergency application, Solicitor General D. John Sauer asked the justices to immediately permit the administration to bar the U.S. Postal Service from sending mail-in ballots to residents of states that have not submitted a list of eligible voters based on citizenship data.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-d337eba2-d91b-4129-9ae0-dba48b25202b"><h3>Election countdown</h3><p>This record does not yet establish one current value.</p></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-5488b575-3a30-44e9-839f-c748807b8570"><h3>Challenging states</h3><p>This record does not yet establish one current value.</p></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-508a9654-0c96-4205-9435-ddd672638724"><h3>Days effective to election</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="story-figure:349410d2bc371635a9b70e1ba8fe0c7f85df7afef4ba22280fae66fe9fbeac65" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="74" data-figure-unit="days">74 days</strong><div class="ledger-calculation" data-computed><p>Computed: November 3, 2026 minus August 21, 2026 = 74 days.</p><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>November 3, 2026 · U.S. District Court for the District of Massachusetts</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>elections occurring before or on November 3, 2026</blockquote><a href="/records/story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384/">Read the source</a></details><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>August 21, 2026 · United States Postal Service</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>Effective August 21, 2026</blockquote><a href="/records/story-pin:78a6944d26561bddfd979798bf3ddd27b2330594118c9fdeea4142f5e6c10fbe/">Read the source</a></details></div></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-4af1f8f9-baf7-4d0d-91d7-f93237671674"><h3>Mail voting availability</h3><p class="ledger-excerpt" data-source-copy>Voting by mail is still available to all voters who are eligible for it in their states, and USPS is expected to deliver mail-in ballots for the midterm election as usual.</p><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:1c5de33c2d400ee09d19a7f325e6164d37468a8d3dcd6b9a2fd275ad73450ff5/" data-passage="Voting by mail is still available to all voters who are eligible for it in their states, and USPS is expected to deliver mail-in ballots for the midterm election as usual." aria-label="Read the source for Mail voting availability">NPR <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-b6a0647a-c8f6-4f09-b6e3-0a6e613c5d89"><h3>Merits ruling status</h3><p class="ledger-excerpt" data-source-copy>But so far, the justices have not ruled on the legality of the order or the USPS plan.</p><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:1c5de33c2d400ee09d19a7f325e6164d37468a8d3dcd6b9a2fd275ad73450ff5/" data-passage="But so far, the justices have not ruled on the legality of the order or the USPS plan." aria-label="Read the source for Merits ruling status">NPR <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-288ee30b-07cb-4158-b501-9d6aa773a36b"><h3>States adopting system</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:38fd0da3dacc5ce6f3afe701ae7f76604d9762fad7fd198254cd2e770c0b0861-865238ee92af5636" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="0" data-figure-unit="states">0 states</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:38fd0da3dacc5ce6f3afe701ae7f76604d9762fad7fd198254cd2e770c0b0861/" data-passage="To date, not a single state has announced that it will do so." aria-label="Read the source for States adopting system">PBS NewsHour <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>To date, not a single state has announced that it will do so.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-fa971d2e-fba0-4297-b172-1ad9ae00f516"><h3>HAVA House votes</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04-65ffeef8400e64f1" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="357" data-figure-unit="votes">357 votes</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04/" data-passage="HAVA, for example, was adopted by the House 357-to-48" aria-label="Read the source for HAVA House votes">Bipartisan current and former members of Congress <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>HAVA, for example, was adopted by the House 357-to-48</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-3052b049-a717-41a6-adad-4979487db5e0"><h3>HAVA Senate votes</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04-e74c0d05bfdb1808" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="92" data-figure-unit="votes">92 votes</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04/" data-passage="the Senate 92-to-2 with sweeping bipartisan majorities." aria-label="Read the source for HAVA Senate votes">Bipartisan current and former members of Congress <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>the Senate 92-to-2 with sweeping bipartisan majorities.</blockquote></details></article><article class="ledger-row" data-state-slot="slot-255c6821-97c8-4e62-aba2-4631f176a257"><h3>UOCAVA ballot deadline</h3><strong class="ledger-value" data-state-figure="occurrence-story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04-61381b0b0c85c38d" data-state-figure-role="current" data-figure-value="45" data-figure-unit="days">45 days</strong><a class="ledger-source" href="/records/story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04/" data-passage="mandated that States give absentee ballots to covered voters at least 45 days before a federal election." aria-label="Read the source for UOCAVA ballot deadline">Bipartisan current and former members of Congress <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="ledger-source-passage"><summary>Recorded passage</summary><blockquote data-source-copy>mandated that States give absentee ballots to covered voters at least 45 days before a federal election.</blockquote></details></article></details><section class="revision-timeline" data-layer="fact" data-revision-confirmations="0" data-revision-changes="0"><details class="source-history"><summary>Source history</summary><p data-revision-no-confirmations>This page does not yet list who reported each figure.</p></details><h2>What changed since</h2><p data-revision-no-changes>No changes are recorded in this view. The first check of this story&#39;s sources has not run yet.</p></section><section data-layer="proof"><h2>Documents</h2><ul><li><a href="/records/story-pin:8b82f7a21920fe4d9bec2bef6b8ac2a65962c1f5593196aac893350f3aa78ebc/" data-source-copy>52 U.S.C. 20302, overseas and military ballots</a> · Original record. This is the statutory text of 52 U.S.C. §20302, the development represented by the selected event.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:1c5de33c2d400ee09d19a7f325e6164d37468a8d3dcd6b9a2fd275ad73450ff5/" data-source-copy>What to know about mail-in voting and Trump&#39;s order</a> · Reference. NPR story reports the administration&#39;s September 2026 request and the status of the mail-voting litigation.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:2784b5d2da64e012b920da0a0d37bbe3b7e60179e56e8d0ad0cdbfbdfcefdf52/" data-source-copy>DOJ makes new appeal for Supreme Court to allow mail voting changes</a> · Reference. The Hill story reports the administration&#39;s September 6 Supreme Court application and the parties&#39; arguments.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:14575e3b949ebee6f583cd8fb6ab816918e2853ae621c759ddfd208779be0c86/" data-source-copy>Trump admin appeals again to Supreme Court to restrict mail-in ballots</a> · Original record. The story reports the administration&#39;s September 2026 Supreme Court appeal concerning mail-ballot restrictions.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:6cf7cea4ff1be8ca259346d6d2fad18109d9f708c06a871f21666c2d9910ba28/" data-source-copy>Application 26A305 for a stay of the September 4 injunction</a> · Original record. The evidence is the September 6, 2026 Supreme Court stay application directly concerning the September 4 preliminary injunction over USPS ballot-mail rules.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:dd309910eda0bb80273688cb45b9dffa7c1446eed03a19675dbfc11e97b27a03/" data-source-copy>Trump administration appeals mail voting decision to Supreme Court</a> · Original record. The evidence reports the Trump administration&#39;s September 2026 appeal to the Supreme Court over mail-ballot restrictions, which is the selected development.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:38fd0da3dacc5ce6f3afe701ae7f76604d9762fad7fd198254cd2e770c0b0861/" data-source-copy>Federal judge extends block on Trump order seeking to limit mail voting in the midterms</a> · Reference. PBS/AP report describing the federal judge&#39;s September 4 preliminary injunction and related mail-voting litigation.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:0c14d0c996eac9302f2fa1f790b57aa88cd75551ec56eb2e7e7d09eb4070e8ab/" data-source-copy>Supreme Court docket 26A305</a> · Original record. The evidence is the Supreme Court&#39;s official docket for application 26A305.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:bd273781aa767102e7a2f0e5fb14554c3064511f7ca07b240db9ec36f71c9384/" data-source-copy>Memorandum and order granting a preliminary injunction</a> · Original record. The document is the September 4, 2026 memorandum and order granting the preliminary injunction.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:57c663c7ac90770794f88e02b605e02e026f11c1888dbb341d4384e489539b58/" data-source-copy>Application 26A297 for a stay of the August 27 temporary restraining order</a> · Original record. The document is the Solicitor General&#39;s September 3, 2026 application for a stay of the district court&#39;s order concerning the USPS ballot-mail rule.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:12998512bbf7032145b2576245d1813fd91e5cfe9c002287571f2acce3c0ec59/" data-source-copy>Postal Service asks Supreme Court to allow Trump&#39;s mail voting changes</a> · Reference. The Hill report is the source evidence describing DOJ&#39;s Supreme Court application and the USPS mail-voting rule litigation.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:8c3f5e01d125c64f39b1f5d0079e6ef06a179807858d468665e7cc3a52b478bc/" data-source-copy>Supreme Court docket 26A297</a> · Original record. The evidence is the Supreme Court&#39;s docket record for application 26A297.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:fd8706f45816b5eed952dc7a6fdf54e2239c1840a2bb9be53822a66f5f24e0ef/" data-source-copy>Per curiam opinion in Trump v. California, 26A124</a> · Original record. The evidence is the Supreme Court&#39;s per curiam opinion and disposition of the stay applications in Trump v. California and Alabama v. California.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:af1dafec4b7202ba84ab9c93e46952de47b88ea567236dd442f3fb78c2e48595/" data-source-copy>Supreme Court docket 26A124</a> · Original record. The evidence is the Supreme Court&#39;s official docket for Application No. 26A124.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:ebb98633d71c6cf640ef2f3b604545916fdd0bfe985508a8b175d0531205aad5/" data-source-copy>Trump administration makes another appeal to Supreme Court to allow mail ballot restrictions</a> · Reference. PBS/AP story reports the September 6, 2026 Supreme Court appeal and related positions; no primary filing was found in document search.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:a1f98307bd569918599841ca56b3be2a577b5e91b6ec073031dd906a0b907596/" data-source-copy>Executive Order 14399</a> · Original record. The evidence is the Federal Register text of Executive Order 14399, the development recorded by the default event.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:de0ff6c5919738b11d41f9b5e02d0701579eaa9202ae3ad43cc374dace78670e/" data-source-copy>2 U.S.C. 7, election day</a> · Original record. This is the Office of the Law Revision Counsel text of 2 U.S.C. §7, the legal record governing the election-day development.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:0ea0045cb705a676a3dc2bc6b67bc08e496f9fa2950e09a94787a7236c9b9d04/" data-source-copy>Amicus brief of bipartisan current and former members of Congress</a> · Original record. This evidence is the amicus brief filed in the Supreme Court matter identified by No. 26A305.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:6512726c9d375de9883f9f6aeaaff8e368d530b5e6285b7b791c3400fcef43fe/" data-source-copy>Letter withdrawing application 26A297</a> · Original record. This DOJ Solicitor General letter is the primary record of the United States withdrawing its September 3 stay application in USPS v. California.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:2d87991b16bc379bd0b08e0377848e56c394460fd80bfa94bd39d29bd5cc1523/" data-source-copy>Opposition to the 26A297 administrative stay</a> · Original record. This is the September 3, 2026 opposition filing in the Supreme Court administrative-stay matter concerning USPS&#39;s federal-election ballot-mail rule.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:cf53f2171dfb5bbbbd73438ab10e06ac00a189f3587ea040501f20ff16be08ee/" data-source-copy>Trump administration makes another Supreme Court appeal on mail ballot fight</a> · Reference. CBS News article reports the September 6 Supreme Court appeal and quotes the filing.</li><li><a href="/records/623afb71e1dbd3ca4087aa98e01f19f132e9ba9477b61a2f3a466fcd66668c41/" data-source-copy>EveryCRSReport</a> · Reference. CRS overview provides corroborating background on the USPS ballot mail rule and litigation.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:e76df51c715bb605096df8547c9411804fdb08f4ff4b83a117cc2456baf4127b/" data-source-copy>Trump administration asks Supreme Court to allow mail ballot restrictions to move forward for a third time</a> · Reference. NBC News reports the administration&#39;s September 6 Supreme Court application.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:d4187bfcfe410e35799a40cbf890a6aa959c0217195fbb8b18dbad36fc51f23d/" data-source-copy>DOJ asks Supreme Court to allow Postal Service rules on mail ballots</a> · Reference. CBS News story reports the DOJ&#39;s September 3 emergency appeal and related USPS mail-ballot litigation.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:dea1c24ad24a3ba6b98f4fb030624477959140608a8932834a382dbe57889776/" data-source-copy>Application 26A124 for a stay of the injunction of Executive Order 14399</a> · Original record. This is the Solicitor General&#39;s July 27, 2026 Supreme Court application and appendix concerning the stay of the Massachusetts injunction against Executive Order 14399.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:78a6944d26561bddfd979798bf3ddd27b2330594118c9fdeea4142f5e6c10fbe/" data-source-copy>Postal Service final rule, Ballot Mail for Federal Elections</a> · Original record. The evidence is the Postal Service&#39;s Federal Register final rule adopting DMM 705.24 for federal ballot mail.</li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:2163dcf85c380fb04c21fb9f0c4d5f9614ef49e898f705fe1d39babf36a7f54d/" data-source-copy>Washington AG Nick Brown release on the preliminary injunction</a> · Original record. This is the Washington A