, 2026 · <span data-source-copy>2 U.S.C. 7, election day</span></li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:dea1c24ad24a3ba6b98f4fb030624477959140608a8932834a382dbe57889776/" data-source-copy>U.S. Department of Justice, Office of the Solicitor General</a> · July 27, 2026 · <span data-source-copy>Application 26A124 for a stay of the injunction of Executive Order 14399</span></li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:e76df51c715bb605096df8547c9411804fdb08f4ff4b83a117cc2456baf4127b/" data-source-copy>NBC News</a> · September 6, 2026 · <span data-source-copy>Trump administration asks Supreme Court to allow mail ballot restrictions to move forward for a third time</span></li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:ebb98633d71c6cf640ef2f3b604545916fdd0bfe985508a8b175d0531205aad5/" data-source-copy>PBS NewsHour</a> · September 6, 2026 · <span data-source-copy>Trump administration makes another appeal to Supreme Court to allow mail ballot restrictions</span></li><li><a href="/records/story-pin:fd8706f45816b5eed952dc7a6fdf54e2239c1840a2bb9be53822a66f5f24e0ef/" data-source-copy>Supreme Court of the United States</a> · August 24, 2026 · <span data-source-copy>Per curiam opinion in Trump v. California, 26A124</span></li></ul></section></main></div><footer class="colophon"><p>Published records carry their review status on the page. Work that has not been published is clearly labeled. Corrections and withdrawals are permanent, dated, and public.</p><p><a href="/">The Catch</a> <a href="/methodology">How we check</a> <a href="/records/">Source library</a></p></footer></div><div id="evidence-preview" class="evidence-preview" popover="manual" role="tooltip"><p class="preview-title"></p><p class="preview-copy"></p><span>Click to read in context</span></div><dialog id="evidence-reader" class="evidence-reader" aria-labelledby="evidence-title"><header class="evidence-toolbar"><span>Source reader</span><div><button type="button" data-expand-evidence aria-label="Expand source reader" aria-pressed="false"><svg 