codex
The strongest omission is now clear: the page’s chronology jumps from March 31 to August 21 and omits the intervening proposed rule, the June and August injunctions, the July appellate ruling, and the district judge’s finding that USPS violated the August 11 injunction and had feigned compliance with the June 25 order. That omitted history directly bears on motive, urgency, equities, and the credibility of the government’s stay request.
