src/pages/events/mail-voting/september-2026.astro-142-        <SourcedBlock source="scotus-26a305-application" kind="record" detail>
src/pages/events/mail-voting/september-2026.astro:143:          <p>The Sunday application asks the Court to stay the September 4 injunction pending appeal to the First Circuit and any later petition, and it asks for an immediate administrative stay, a short pause while the justices decide the full request. Sauer writes that the rule imposes "modest envelope-design and addressee-information requirements", and that states remain responsible for who may vote by mail.<Cite s="scotus-26a305-application" passage="addressee-information requirements" /></p></SourcedBlock>
