   245	address, and unique IMb associated with every voter who will receive a mail ballot.
   246	91 Fed. Reg. 54991. Per the Postal Service’s plans, as revealed by the Disclosure,
   247	there is then an initial verification step that appears nowhere in the text of the Rule:
   248	Before election officials can even bring outgoing bulk mailings of ballots to a postal
   249	facility for mailing, they must upload a manifest with the names of the intended
   250	recipients, and match that manifest with the data in the Portal. Disclosure ¶¶ 11–12.
   251	A mismatch means the ballots do not pass Go. Id.
   252	The second verification point occurs when election officials bring a batch of
   253	outgoing mail ballots to a postal facility. There, Postal Service employees are to scan
   254	barcodes and confirm that they match the Portal’s data. 91 Fed. Reg. 54981. The Rule
   255	describes this step as “straightforward.” Id. It says that “[s]canning a barcode
